Work done in blowing a soap bubble

\[
\begin{align*}
&= \text{surface energy of the bubble} \\
&= \text{surface area } \times \gamma \\
&= 2 \times 4 \pi r^2 \times \gamma \, (\text{since bubble has two surfaces, total surface area} = 2 \times 4 \pi r^2) \\
&= 2 \times 4 \times \pi \times 10^2 \, \text{cm}^2 \times 30 \, \text{dynes/cm} = \mathbf{75398.22 \, \text{ergs}}
\end{align*}
\]
